    "⌘↩ runs" : {

    },
    "0 draws all of them. Copy, export, find and sort always use the whole value." : {

    },
    "0 in all three leaves the server's own settings alone." : {

    },
    "0 is one transaction for the whole file, which is what Pharos has always done — nothing lands until everything does. A number commits as it goes, so the batches that finished stay on the server even if a later row stops the import." : {

    },
    "0 keeps it until the connection closes, which is what Pharos has always done." : {

    },
    "0 keeps them for as long as the maximum lifetime allows." : {

    },
    "0 lets DuckDB use every core." : {

    },
    "0 turns Pharos's timeout off: a query then runs until it ends or you cancel it. On PostgreSQL the server's own statement_timeout still applies." : {

    },
